explicit blank; rejected if OS label is nonblank}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
Use the same bracketed volume name each time you scan the same drive. For example, use [Backup-1]E:\\Music on Windows or [Backup-1]/mnt/e/Music on WSL/Linux for the same external drive. If no bracketed prefix is supplied, TLO resolves and uses the operating-system volume label when it can. The default labels New Volume and Local Disk are treated as blank rather than as useful unique volume names.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
TLO tracks inventory by visible volume name plus the path below the volume. It ignores and does not store the drive letter or WSL /mnt/<drive> prefix in bootlist.csv or the top SEARCH_PATH log headers. For example, [Backup-1]/mnt/e/Music and [Backup-1]/mnt/n/Music are treated as the same stored root [Backup-1] /Music when they refer to the same labeled volume.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- If no bracketed volume name is supplied, TLO substitutes the operating-system volume label for logging and existing-volume comparison when that label can be resolved. The default Windows-style labels New Volume and Local Disk are treated as blank rather than as useful volume names.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- If an explicit bracketed volume name is supplied, it must match the mounted drive label when that label can be resolved. A mismatch raises an alert and that path is not processed.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- For a labeled drive, TLO no longer asks whether to skip or re-inventory when it sees the same volume again. It applies the path relationship automatically: same path or parent path replaces that scope; child path replaces only entries below that child path; non-overlapping paths on the same volume are added to the same volume log header and appended.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
After a path-scoped re-inventory, TLO prints a concise re-inventory reconciliation line. TLOHome/logs/reinventoryDelta.log contains the full old-to-new audit: each previous bootlist row is labeled UNCHANGED, METADATA_CHANGED, RENAMED, RENAMED_METADATA_CHANGED, SPLIT, MERGED, REGROUPED, CORRUPTION_REMOVED, UNRESOLVED, or MISSING, with old/current Show and path values plus the reason. Current rows with no previous-row match are listed as NEW. The log also retains the overall previous/prepared/Stage 3/corruption/unresolved/final-row counts. summary.log receives the compact counts and disposition totals instead of repeating every per-row detail block. This makes a genuine disappearance stand out as MISSING instead of being hidden by a net row count.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Explicit [] means an explicit blank volume. It is rejected when the mounted drive has a nonblank, non-default operating-system volume label.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- For drives with a blank volume label, or with the default labels New Volume or Local Disk, TLO uses one append-only blank-volume log set. The log header is SEARCH_PATH: [] with no path. There is no skip or re-inventory for blank/default-label drives, so you must avoid or clean up duplicates yourself if the same blank/default-label drive content is scanned multiple times.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- When more than one path is queued, TLO schedules labeled volumes first. Paths on the same named physical drive run serially; different physical drives may run in parallel according to Performance Mode and Max Workers. After labeled work completes, all blank-label paths run serially in drive-letter order.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- A single labeled volume log can list multiple SEARCH_PATH header lines when you add non-overlapping roots from the same drive over time.}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx8640\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa20{\loch
Mount aliases: TLO rejects obvious duplicate and overlapping roots after normalization, but symlinks, junctions, case-sensitive aliases, and OS-specific mount aliases can still create duplicates if they point to the same content.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Required Search Path and optional control files}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
Search Path is required for every full inventory run. Enter one direct inventory root or multiple entries separated by semicolons. Each direct entry may use the same optional [Volume] prefix and per-path directives shown below. A Search Path entry that ends in .txt is treated as an inventory-control file; the file may have any filename and uses the former toBeInventoried.txt format, with one inventory root per non-comment line. Blank lines and lines whose first non-whitespace character is # are ignored, and lines beginning with REM are also comments. TLOHome/toBeInventoried.txt is never read automatically; COMPLETE packages continue to include it only as an example/template. To use that template, explicitly enter its fully qualified filename in Search Path.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Windows root-path examples can be entered as E:, E:\\, or H:.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
For WSL/Linux full inventory, Windows drive paths are translated to /mnt/<drive>/... while preserving the full subtree. Paths such as D:\\B-J\\D\\Dudek, Les are valid; the comma in the folder name is part of the path and should not cause TLO to scan only /mnt/d.}
\par \pard\plain \s72\rtlch\af12\afs17\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af8\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb40\sa80\ltrpar\cf0\f8\fs17\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af13\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb60\sa120{\loch
REM examples for Windows\line [External-E]E:\line [External-E]E:\\\line [Archive-H]H:\line [Backup-1]E:\\Music\line [Archive-F]F:\\boots --$slam "Bob Dylan"\line [Archive-G]G:\\incoming --$copy H:\\TaggedCopies\line [Archive-I]I:\\new --$copy-delete J:\\TaggedFinished --$slam "Bill Dickens"\line \line REM examples for WSL/Linux\line [Backup-1]/mnt/e/Music\line [Archive-F]/mnt/f/boots --$slam "Bob Dylan"\line [Archive-G]/mnt/g/incoming --$copy /mnt/h/TaggedCopies\line [Archive-I]/mnt/i/new --$copy-delete /mnt/j/TaggedFinished --$slam "Bill Dickens"}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Optional per-path directives can be added after the path. Use --$slam ARTIST_NAME to force an artist, --$copy DESTINATION to copy and tag that path's folders at the destination, or --$copy-delete DESTINATION to copy/move, verify when needed, delete the original, and tag the transferred folders. Legacy -$slam still works.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- The order of --$slam and the copy directive does not matter, but a single line cannot contain both --$copy and --$copy-delete. Destination folders must already exist and must be fully qualified paths.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Before inventory starts, TLO checks whether each copy destination has enough free space for the source root or roots assigned to it. If a destination is short on space, TLO stops and reports the destination, the affected source path or paths, and how much additional space is needed.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- When this capacity check is needed, the console first prints a Note explaining that TLO is checking source folder sizes before it checks destination capacity. Large roots can take a while to total, similar to opening folder Properties.}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx8640\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Volume label behavior: If no bracketed prefix is supplied, TLO uses the operating-system volume label for comparison and logging when available. Use [Volume] only when it matches the mounted drive label. Use [] only when an explicitly blank volume is intended and the mounted drive label is blank or unavailable.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
9. Running the main GUI}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
Start the Windows GUI with TLOHome/apps/Windows/tlo-ggi.exe, or the WSL/Linux GUI from TLOHome/apps/Linux. The GUI can also be preloaded with command-line arguments such as --TLOHome, --search-path, --compliant, --as-is-artist-name, --etree-lookup, --setlistfm-lookup, --setlistfm-upgrade, --thorough-setlist-matching, --corrupt-files, --corrupt-folders, --corrupt-folder-threshold, --performance-mode, and --max-workers. The main Inventory and Search windows do not show an editable TLOHome box; the startup value is used for the whole session. In the main Inventory window, the resolved TLOHome appears on the same top row as the application title, immediately to the left of the hamburger menu. The required Search Path field is labeled Path(s). Its entry accepts semicolon-separated direct roots and .txt control-file paths. One-line checkbox labels are vertically aligned with their indicators; wrapped checkbox labels keep the indicator aligned with the first text line. Slam is labeled Slam (optional); its entry is approximately half its previous width and applies to direct Search Path entries. The header and top option rows use minimal vertical spacing.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
On native Windows installations, drag one or more folders and/or .txt control files from File Explorer onto the Path(s) text box. TLO processes the complete Windows drag payload, so every item selected in one drag is retained. Each drag appends its items to the existing Search Path value in drop order, with semicolons inserted automatically. You can drag one folder, then another, then several folders together; all remain in Search Path. Build 463 also acknowledges each successful Windows drop to TkDND so a later drag does not replace the accumulated value. A .txt file is preserved as the control-file path. Other dropped files contribute their containing folder. If a dropped path itself contains a semicolon, TLO quotes that path automatically so it remains one Search Path entry.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
The upper-right hamburger menu includes Donate. Donate > Venmo displays @James-Scarano-3. Donate > Check displays James Scarano, 49 Majestic Ave., Nashua, NH 03063. Venmo and Check are submenu items with chevrons. Their detail rows use normal dark menu text instead of disabled gray text.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
The GUI and CLI share the same defaults through the internal option registry. setlist.fm still depends on etreeDB: command-line startup rejects --setlistfm-lookup unless --etree-lookup is also supplied, and the GUI automatically selects etreeDB when setlist.fm is selected.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
When you click Inventory, the Inventory button grays out immediately, Tag and Add Shows are disabled, and the output pane reports that the request was accepted while TLO prepares the roots. Existing labeled-volume overlap is resolved automatically from the same/parent/child/non-overlap path rules; TLO does not ask a Skip/Re-inventory question. Ctrl-A (Control-A) selects all text in the main output console. Ctrl-A also selects the complete contents of every editable text input field throughout the Inventory GUI, Tagger, Search, Artist DB Search, and dialogs, including fields created after the main window opens.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
The main Inventory window also includes a Research button. Clicking Research opens a text-entry dialog for an artist followed by a date, a venue, or a date. Search opens the result in a separate scrollable text window. Research is read-only and searches TLOHome/logs/meta*.log plus related comp*.log entries using the same engine as the standalone tlo-research app.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Folder reversal is intentionally separate from the Inventory GUI. Use the standalone tlo-reverse CLI with one fully qualified path identifying the original folder, current folder, or containing path to reverse. TLO reads successful folder-operation mappings from TLOHome/logs and infers whether the operation was Rename Compliantly, Tag Copy, or Tag Copy/Delete Original; no copy-versus-rename flag is normally needed. Copy/Delete is restored to the exact logged original location/name, whether or not Rename Compliantly was enabled. Rename-only is renamed back. Tag Copy leaves the original in place and removes only the exact logged copy after confirming that the source and copy still contain the same relative file-name set. Audio tags are never changed or reversed. If a broad path matches more than one currently applicable run, tlo-reverse stops instead of guessing; enter a narrower path or use --log. Use --dry-run to see the selected log and exact folder actions without changing anything. Results are appended to TLOHome/logs/reverseFolders.log.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
If you click Quit while a full inventory scan is active, TLO warns that cleanup may take a moment, then requests cancellation and stops active workers. Cancellation cleanup removes only tokenized log files newly allocated by that interrupted run; a token/log set reused from an earlier inventory is preserved. Token values are validated before cleanup so a malformed value cannot escape TLOHome/logs. If scanning has already finished but cleanup, sibling-collection aggregation, or output generation is still running, TLO warns before a forced exit that an in-progress collection move can be interrupted. Collection moves are journaled, and the next normal Inventory run attempts automatic rollback before scanning.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

