Full Inventory mode that copies identified music folders and tags the copies.}\cell\row\pard \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx4643\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx9824\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Tag Copy/Delete Original}\cell\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Full Inventory mode that copies or moves identified folders, verifies cross-partition copies, and removes originals only after verification.}\cell\row\pard \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx4643\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx9824\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Dry run}\cell\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Non-destructive metadata and tag planning selected on the main Inventory window and inherited by Inventory, Tag, and Add Shows.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
19. GitHub update checks and Auto update}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Check for updates compares the installed build with the latest public GitHub release and downloads only the exact operating-system/package-layout match to Downloads. It prefers the matching update ZIP and falls back to the matching complete ZIP only when that update ZIP is absent. Generic/source ZIPs and the other Windows layout are never substitutes. TLO does not install or extract the update automatically.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Normal update checks are pinned to the official onaracstlo-lab/TradersLittleOrganizer repository; environment variables cannot redirect the update source. Redirects are accepted only when they remain on approved GitHub HTTPS hosts. Downloads are streamed with a 1 GiB hard safety ceiling and stop immediately if received data exceeds the release-declared size or the ceiling. A release ZIP must also have a valid published SHA-256 digest; a missing or mismatched digest is a verification failure, not a successful update.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Auto update is a download-only startup check. Its setting is stored in TLOHome/update-settings.json, and automatic checks are limited to at most once per day. After download, TLO verifies the package manifest matches the expected build, package kind, and exact platform/layout and verifies that the manifest database declaration matches the ZIP contents.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- A release may provide both package types (eight assets), only the four complete ZIPs, or only the four update ZIPs. The updater handles any of these cases and uses only the exact package for the installed platform/layout.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Complete packages include the platform applications, required TLO_DBs files, manual, FAQ, starter files, work folders, manifests, checksums, and scan receipts. Update packages always omit user inventory/output areas. By default they also omit databases; an update may explicitly include only TLO_DBs/artists.sqlite and TLO_DBs/venues.txt. TLO tells you when the downloaded update contains those database master files because applying it will replace them.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- TLO detects Windows onefile versus Windows onedir from the installed layout and will not download the other layout as a fallback. Do not overlay a Windows onefile apps/Windows folder with a Windows onedir folder or vice versa. Replace apps/Windows as a unit only when deliberately switching layouts; onedir executables require the shared _internal folder.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Close all TLO applications before applying an update.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\pagebb\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa240{\loch\fs28\b\loch
20. Duplicate-folder cleanup utility - tlo-deleteDupes}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
tlo-deleteDupes searches one fully qualified Input Path recursively for duplicate sibling folders. Candidate discovery combines exact copy families and same-artist/date matching. An exact copy family includes folders such as X, X (copy2), and X (copy3), so numbered copies are compared with one another even when X is absent or has different contents. TLO also compares same-parent folders when their normalized artist and date match even if the rest of the folder names differ.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
Candidate folders are divided into content-equivalence clusters after TLO compares their complete recursive manifests. Copies are compared with one another as well as with unsuffixed folders. Each cluster of two or more identical trees keeps one folder and moves the other identical members. TLO prefers to keep a folder without a terminal (copyN) suffix. If more than one unsuffixed folder in the cluster is identical, the alphabetically first name is kept. If a cluster contains only numbered copies, the lowest-numbered copy is kept. Different content clusters remain as separate variants. For example, if X differs from X (copy2) and X (copy3), but copy2 and copy3 match one another, TLO keeps X and copy2 and moves copy3.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
Same-artist/date discovery recognizes a standalone four-digit 19xx/20xx year, yyyy-mm-dd style dates (including xx month/day components), and four-digit-year ranges. An unknown date without an actual four-digit year is not enough to broaden duplicate discovery. A matching artist and date is only a way to select folders for comparison; it does not by itself make a folder a duplicate.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
Before any candidate folder is moved, TLO requires the same relative nested folder structure, including empty folders, and the same relative file names and file sizes as another member of its content-equivalence cluster. This cleanup utility deliberately does not compare file bytes or timestamps when deciding whether folders are duplicates. A folder whose manifest differs remains in its own content cluster rather than being discarded merely because another folder was previously chosen as a master.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
When two folders in the same candidate component do not match, TLO appends one short CSV line to TLOHome/deleteDupesMismatches.txt. Copies are compared with one another as well as with unsuffixed folders. The three fields are folder name, folder name, simple reason. Examples include different number of files, different sub-structure, different file names, and 01.flac different sizes. Only folder names are recorded; full paths are not included. Folder names containing commas are automatically CSV-quoted. deletedDirs.txt remains only the list of folders actually moved.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
Before any duplicate member of a content-equivalence cluster is moved into the duplicates holding folder, TLO checks every FLAC file in that cluster's kept folder tree by fully decoding its audio stream with the bundled ffmpeg validator. This is a full audio-integrity check, not merely a FLAC header or tag read.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
Each full FLAC decode has a 180-second timeout. A timeout means the keeper is unverifiable, not healthy or corrupt. If any kept-folder FLAC times out, TLO reports the condition and leaves that entire duplicate cluster in place rather than relocating its other members.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch
If a FLAC in the kept folder is confirmed corrupt, TLO looks for the same relative file in other members of that same content-equivalence cluster. Copy-suffixed repair sources are tried in numeric order: copy1, copy2, copy3, and so on. Qualifying unsuffixed repair sources are tried alphabetically. A candidate replacement must fully decode successfully, is staged separately, byte-verified before installation, and is decoded again after replacement.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch
If no healthy replacement is available for a confirmed-corrupt keeper FLAC, or if keeper validation is unverifiable because of timeout, I/O/resource, or validator-infrastructure failure, TLO leaves that duplicate cluster in place for later review. An unverifiable validation attempt is not treated as proof that the file is healthy or corrupt. Duplicate relocation proceeds only when the selected keeper is fully verified or successfully repaired.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
TLO places qualifying duplicates in a folder named duplicates at the root of the partition containing the Input Path. TLO creates that folder when it does not already exist. On Windows, E:\\Music therefore uses E:\\duplicates. On Linux/macOS, a search under /mnt/music uses /mnt/music/duplicates when /mnt/music is the filesystem mount root. TLO moves the entire qualifying duplicate folder tree in one same-partition directory move; it does not move child files individually. If an entry with the same name already exists in duplicates, TLO preserves both by adding a collision suffix such as (moved 2). If the search includes the partition root, TLO excludes the duplicates holding folder from further duplicate discovery. After a successful move, TLO appends the folder's full original pre-move path to TLOHome/deletedDirs.txt.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
TLOHome is resolved using the same --TLOHome and TLOHome environment-variable logic used by the other TLO mains. The compatibility alias remains accepted but is intentionally omitted from user-facing help and documentation. The Input Path itself must be a fully qualified existing directory.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
Example: tlo-deleteDupes.cmd --TLOHome C:\\TLOHome E:\\Music}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
On Linux or macOS source execution: python3 tlo-deleteDupes.py --TLOHome /path/to/TLOHome /path/to/music}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
Ctrl-C stops further work. The program closes deletedDirs.txt and deleteDupesMismatches.txt while unwinding and exits with cancellation status 130. Entries successfully logged before the interrupt remain in their respective log files; any folder already moved into the partition-root duplicates holding folder remains there.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs22\b0\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\pagebb\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa240{\loch\fs28\b\loch
21. Research log lookup - tlo-research}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
Research provides a focused way to inspect the metadata and complete-path evidence already recorded in TLOHome/logs. The same search engine is used by the standalone tlo-research console application and by the Research button on the main Inventory GUI.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
The input string is one of three forms: an artist followed by a date, a venue, or a date. Examples are Grateful Dead 1977-05-08, Barton Hall, 1977-05-08, and xxxx-xx-xx. Research uses the same canonical date parser as Inventory, so every Inventory-supported date representation is accepted, including numeric dates, textual-month dates, compact dates, slash dates, supported year ranges, same-month multi-day ranges such as 1970-04-12-13, 1970-04-12,13, and 12-13 April 1970, partial x-placeholder forms such as 2001-04-1x, 2004-0x-xx, 202x-xx-xx, 19xx-xx-xx, 20xx-xx-xx, and xxxx-xx-xx, plus a standalone four-digit 19xx/20xx year. A valid same-month multi-day range is normalized to its first day for matching; all days must be valid and strictly ascending. Research normalizes the date before matching. A date-only search matches the DATE field; artist plus date requires both ARTIST and DATE. Any other input is treated as a venue and is matched case-insensitively against VENUE.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
Research reads every meta*.log in TLOHome/logs and returns the complete SHOW_NAME through END_SHOW_METADATA block for every matching record. It then uses MAIN_DIR_PATH and MUSIC_DIRS_JSON to locate every corresponding path line in comp*.log and displays those under COMP LOG. Research does not stop after the first metadata match. After the structured results, it performs a second exhaustive raw-line scan of every meta*.log and comp*.log and displays an ALL RELATED RAW LOG LINES section with every directly related occurrence, its log filename, and its line number. There is no per-file or per-query hit limit. This raw evidence is displayed even when there are zero structured metadata matches, which makes it possible to trace historical source strings or intermediate evidence that did not survive into the final metadata record.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
In the Inventory GUI, click Research and type the research string in the input box. Search remains the active/default action whenever the Research dialog is active, so Return or keypad Enter anywhere in that dialog runs the search. Results open in a read-only, non-wrapping text window with vertical scrolling and a horizontal scrollbar along the bottom. Ctrl-A selects the complete result even when a button owns focus. The results window has a Search button, and Ctrl-F invokes the same action. The find dialog has a Search for: box and mutually exclusive Forward and Backwards choices, with Forward selected by default. Repeated searches continue in the chosen direction, ignore case, and wrap to the opposite end when there is no later/earlier match. The GUI uses the TLOHome already resolved when the Inventory app started.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
In the CLI, output is written to the console. TLOHome can be supplied with --TLOHome; otherwise the TLOHome environment variable is used. The standalone app follows the same hidden compatibility precedence as the other TLO mains.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa160{\loch\fs22\b0\loch
